{"id": "section-body-13724", "title": "Glaucoma", "chapterId": "chapter-fourteen", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "EYE DISEASES AND REFRACTIVE ERRORS", "Major Blinding Eye Diseases", "Glaucoma"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-13724", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Glaucoma", "runs": [{"text": "Glaucoma"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "1312"}}, {"id": "body-13725", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Glaucoma is a syndrome characterized by optic nerve damage and peripheral visual field loss which may be associated with raised intraocular pressure. The main classes of glaucoma are open angle glaucoma and angle closure glaucoma.", "runs": [{"text": "Glaucoma is a syndrome characterized by optic nerve damage and peripheral"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "visual field loss which may be associated with raised intraocular pressure. The main classes of glaucoma are open angle glaucoma and angle closure glaucoma."}]}, {"id": "body-13726-textbox1-00001", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Normal", "text": "Note:", "runs": [{"text": "Note:", "bold": true}]}, {"id": "body-13726-textbox1-00002", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Glaucoma may be congenital, primary or secondary to ocular or systemic conditions", "runs": [{"text": "Glaucoma"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "may"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "congenital,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "primary"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "secondary"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ocular"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "systemic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "conditions"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1308"}}, {"id": "body-13726-textbox1-00003", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "By Far POAG is the commonest type of Glaucoma in adults", "runs": [{"text": "By"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Far"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "POAG"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "commonest"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "type"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Glaucoma"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "adults"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1308"}}, {"id": "body-13726-textbox1-00004", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "AACG is a different entity and should be managed as ocular emergency", "runs": [{"text": "AACG"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "different"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "entity"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "should"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "managed"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "as"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ocular"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "emergency"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1308"}}, {"id": "body-13726-textbox1-00005", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Congenital Glaucoma can present with simple symptoms and needs high clinical acumen for diagnosis and treatment. So, they should be referred to center with capacity to manage congenital Glaucoma", "runs": [{"text": "Congenital"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Glaucoma"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "can"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "present"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "simple"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "symptoms"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "needs"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "high"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "acumen"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "diagnosis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and treatment. So, they should be referred to center with capacity to manage congenital Glaucoma"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1308"}}], "source": {"file": "medical.docx", "chapter": "Eye diseases and refractive errors", "start": "body-13724", "end": "body-13726-